(And non-cursed armour is always +0 or better.)

The actual numbers are somewhat complicated, but if my maths is
correct, the chance of a piece of armour (other than lev boots, HoOA,
or fumbling) known to have been generated uncursed having been
generated with positive enchantment is 505/8686, about 6%. The
corresponding figure for armour that was generated blessed is
1010/1919, a little over 50%.

(The _amount_ of any positive enchantment isn't dependent on the
blessed status; it's an exponential distribution capped at 5 or XL/3,
whichever is higher.)

